---
import BlogPost from '../../components/BlogPost.astro';

const link = (href: string) =>
  `font-semibold text-plum underline decoration-plum/40 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-plum`;
---

<BlogPost
  title="Introducing the Attirel Size Guide Library"
  description="Eight brand fit guides, bra sizing, international conversions, and inseam lengths: a complete, free sizing reference library, launching today."
  heading="Introducing the Attirel Size Guide Library"
  date="2026-07-20"
  readingTime="3 min read"
  ctaHeading="Guides answer the general question. The app answers yours."
  ctaBody="Attirel matches your exact measurements to the right size across 100+ brands. It's the interactive companion to everything in this library."
>
  <p>
    Every size label is a small act of translation: from your body, to a measurement, to a
    number that means something different at every store in the mall. Most of us handle that
    translation by guessing, and the guessing shows: closets with three "mediums" in three
    different actual sizes, and a steady rhythm of returns.
  </p>
  <p>
    Today we're shipping something we've wanted to exist for a long time: a complete, free
    sizing reference library. No email gates, no ten-paragraph preambles. Just direct answers
    to the questions people actually type into search bars at 11pm with a full cart.
  </p>

  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Eight brands, honestly assessed</h2>
  <p>
    The heart of the library is a set of brand fit guides. Each one opens with a straight
    verdict (runs small, runs large, true to size), then backs it up with how the brand
    behaves category by category, standard international conversions, and the questions
    shoppers ask most:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
    <li><a href="/size-guides/uniqlo-size-chart-fit-guide/" class={link('')}>Uniqlo</a>: the slim Japanese cut, explained</li>
    <li><a href="/size-guides/levis-size-chart-fit-guide/" class={link('')}>Levi's</a>: stretch vs. rigid, and when to size up</li>
    <li><a href="/size-guides/adidas-size-chart-fit-guide/" class={link('')}>Adidas</a>: why so many people size down in Originals</li>
    <li><a href="/size-guides/gap-size-chart-fit-guide/" class={link('')}>Gap</a>: American vanity sizing at work</li>
    <li><a href="/size-guides/shein-size-chart-fit-guide/" class={link('')}>Shein</a>: navigating famously inconsistent sizing</li>
    <li><a href="/size-guides/lululemon-size-chart-fit-guide/" class={link('')}>Lululemon</a>: compression fit and the numeric system</li>
    <li><a href="/size-guides/mango-size-chart-fit-guide/" class={link('')}>Mango</a>: the slim European block, decoded</li>
    <li><a href="/size-guides/asos-size-chart-fit-guide/" class={link('')}>ASOS</a>: one true-to-size house brand, 850+ wildcards</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Three references you'll keep coming back to</h2>
  <p>
    Around the brand guides sit three evergreen references. The
    <a href="/size-guides/international-size-conversion/" class={link('')}>international size
    conversion charts</a> translate between US, UK, EU, AU, and JP systems for clothing and
    shoes. The <a href="/size-guides/bra-size-calculator-guide/" class={link('')}>bra size
    guide</a> demystifies band math, cup letters, and sister sizes, with a worked example
    instead of hand-waving. And the
    <a href="/size-guides/jeans-inseam-length-guide/" class={link('')}>jeans inseam &amp; length
    guide</a> finally answers what those petite, regular, and tall labels mean in actual inches.
  </p>

  <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Why static guides, when we build a fit app?</h2>
  <p>
    Because the two solve different halves of the problem. A guide can tell you that Uniqlo
    tends to run a size small or that Adidas Originals run large — the brand-level pattern.
    What it can't know is <em>you</em>: your measurements, your fit preferences, the difference
    between how you want a tee and a trucker jacket to sit. That's the half the
    <a href="https://www.attirel.ai" class={link('')}>Attirel app</a> handles, matching your
    exact measurements against specific garments across 100+ brands.
  </p>
  <p>
    Start with the guides. When you're ready for answers about your own wardrobe,
    <a href="/app/" class={link('')}>the app is the interactive companion</a>. And if you're
    not sure of your measurements in the first place, our
    <a href="/how-to-measure/" class={link('')}>how-to-measure guide</a> takes ten minutes and
    a soft tape measure.
  </p>
  <p>
    The library grows from here: more brands, more categories. If there's a brand whose sizing
    keeps burning you, we'd like to hear about it.
  </p>
</BlogPost>
